136:- **Target evidence root.** An **empty** evidence root. When it already exists, its owner is taken as the account of the API and the worker (see "Ownership of the restored evidence" below).
144:  [--readyz-url http://127.0.0.1:3000/readyz] [--evidence-owner <uid>:<gid>]
147:**Ownership of the restored evidence.** The API and the worker run without any capability (`cap_drop: ALL`), so they can read and remove only the evidence files their own account owns. `restore.sh` therefore gives every restored evidence directory and file to that account, with mode `0700` for directories and `0600` for files, the modes the filesystem store writes itself. You do **not** need a separate `chown` step.
149:- **Which account.** By default, the owner of the existing, empty target evidence root. In Compose this is the image's app user, uid `10001`, which owns the evidence volume. If the root does not exist yet, the account that runs `restore.sh` creates it and keeps it. `--evidence-owner <uid>:<gid>` names the account explicitly, for example `--evidence-owner 10001:10001`. Any other value is refused: `BLOCKED: --evidence-owner must be <uid>:<gid> (numbers), for example 10001:10001` (exit 2).
